                  "branchResults": [],
                  "explanation": "At the declared entry, the outcome is conditional because token existence and expiry are unspecified. If the supplied token resolves to an active share, the handler obtains that share's memo ID, rejects only missing/non-normal/SPACE memos at this visible entry, and builds a read context using that same memo ID as the shared-memo binding. The visible access control treats the share as applicable when the memo ID equals the shared-memo ID and the memo is not SPACE, returning an allowed private read decision; the handler then returns the converted memo with Parent cleared. Invalid or expired tokens return NOT_FOUND before memo retrieval. The specified entry also visibly returns NOT_FOUND for a missing, non-normal, or SPACE memo, and for read-context resolution/access denial; creator-conversion failure for a missing creator is another visible NOT_FOUND path. The premises establish the described memo properties only conditional on token resolution, not that resolution occurs. Therefore no single concrete allow/deny outcome can be selected without observing whether the token exists and is unexpired; an observation of an active resolved share would decide the requested conditional path, while an absent or expired share would decide the NOT_FOUND path.",
